{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/getmonotonictime()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"getMonotonicTime"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gint64","text":"gint64","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The monotonic clock will always increase and doesn’t suffer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"discontinuities when the user (or NTP) changes the system time.  It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"may or may not continue to tick during times where the machine is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"suspended.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"We try to use the clock that corresponds as closely as possible to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the passage of time as measured by system calls such as","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"man:poll(2)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" but it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"may not always be possible to do this.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A more accurate version of this function exists."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.get_monotonic_time_ns"},{"type":"text","text":"] returns the time in nanoseconds."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Function","symbolKind":"func","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"getMonotonicTime"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gint64","text":"gint64","k